1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:08,667
COMMONKIT: Share and manage community machines. Book access. Fund upkeep. Earn usage rights.

2
00:00:08,867 --> 00:00:13,867
Book: Book a shared printer: a usage fee for upkeep, plus a refundable deposit.

3
00:00:14,167 --> 00:00:18,400
Book: Recorded testnet booking: Alex's two-slot reservation.

4
00:00:19,467 --> 00:00:24,267
Care: A bridge checks the booking and reports usage. These devices are emulated.

5
00:00:24,267 --> 00:00:28,667
Care: A due rule lets the printer's agent open an upkeep task. Demo: 30 min; production: 200 h.

6
00:00:28,667 --> 00:00:33,933
Independent approval: Ava cleaned the nozzle. A test print passed, and Mark independently approved her work.

7
00:00:33,933 --> 00:00:36,767
Earn access: She earned two non-transferable usage-right NFTs.

8
00:00:37,067 --> 00:00:43,233
Use the reward: Ava used right-3 for this booking: zero usage fee. The refundable deposit still applies.

9
00:00:43,233 --> 00:00:47,367
Use the reward: After the session, the right was consumed. Her care earned access.

10
00:00:48,433 --> 00:00:53,267
A machine with a budget: Each machine runs its own keyless NEAR account, with a capped operating budget.

11
00:00:53,267 --> 00:00:56,633
A machine with a budget: Excess fees go back to the community's Sputnik DAO.

12
00:00:56,633 --> 00:01:00,667
The machine opens a proposal: For a larger purchase, the printer itself opened proposal #10.

13
00:01:00,667 --> 00:01:05,433
The machine opens a proposal: The council approved it. The DAO paid the demo supplier 4 testnet NEAR.

14
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:12,700
Verify it: Inspect the live checks: eight keyless accounts, matching machine code hashes, balanced ledgers.

15
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:17,833
Verify it: Or run the verifier. No wallet, no keys. COMMONKIT: care earns access.
